FILE-05: round control times to the nearest second when reading them

controldata() converts a control's time from hours to seconds with
(long)(3600.0 * time), which truncates. A time read as h:mm:ss can come
out just below the whole second (0:01:01 gives 60.99999999999999 s, so
60 s), and the writer's "%.4f HOURS" rounds 45 % of times down by up to
0.18 s, so they lose a second on reload. Round instead, as timedata()
already does for [TIMES]. Four decimals of an hour are 0.36 s, so a
rounded time always comes back to the second that was saved.

Apply from the root of an EPANET checkout at 83e25bb:
    git apply FILE-05_fix.patch

diff --git a/src/input3.c b/src/input3.c
index e97110f..3800ebe 100644
--- a/src/input3.c
+++ b/src/input3.c
@@ -1039,7 +1039,7 @@ int controldata(Project *pr)
     control->Type = ctltype;
     control->Status = status;
     control->Setting = setting;
-    control->Time = (long)(3600.0 * time);
+    control->Time = (long)(3600.0 * time + 0.5);
     if (ctltype == TIMEOFDAY) control->Time %= SECperDAY;
     control->Grade = level;
     control->isEnabled = isEnabled;
